WEBVTT

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.000
Oh, there's some more over there.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.130
What on earth?

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.550
An egg... house?

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.130
Welcome, stranger.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:36.590
Who are you?!

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.270
I am Jada.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:44.890
That is my humble abode and place of work.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:53.030
Welcome to the Jade Egg Salon.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.570
A beautician... Are you really?

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:02.750
Whether you believe it or not is up to you.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.000
<i>Well, why not?</i>

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.380
Can you give me a haircut?

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.800
Oh? You mean it?

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:16.180
I had planned on taking the day off today, but... oh well.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:18.890
Make way for a customer!

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.390
Why is that necessary?

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:25.350
Wow...

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.190
I'm going to straighten up a bit, so hold on just a sec.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.360
Are these what you use for work?

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.570
That's right. I cut hair and such.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:41.830
I guess it really <i>is</i> a salon.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.580
You certainly do speak your mind.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.960
Okay, we've got a spot open for you now. Have a seat.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:49.830
Thanks.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.170
What kind of egg is this?

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.590
An ostrich egg, maybe?

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.090
Why doesn't it fall over?

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.640
Okay, that's enough questions from you.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.770
It's my turn now. What kind of cut do you want?

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.440
Oh... I'll let you decide.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:11.900
My, you're a brave soul.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.020
I am?

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.320
A mohawk it is, then. I'll get the razor ready!

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.070
Sorry. I'll decide for myself after all.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.120
Aw.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.250
I don't really know what to pick...

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:31.630
Are you sure you're not interested in the mohawk?

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.340
A mohawk... Just imagine...

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.550
Make it short.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.550
Take it all the way down. Just like yours.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:46.180
Deary me. Are you sure?

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.940
It looks really light, and I think that's cute.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.900
Oh, my!

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.900
You little charmer, you!
Flattery won't get you anywhere, you know.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.400
What's with that tone?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.450
Here, have a candy.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.950
So it <i>did</i> get me somewhere.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.990
Well, first of all, I'll get your hair nice and wet.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.040
Okie dokes.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.170
Chestnut-san.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.380
It's "Hakumei."

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.750
Hakumei, you have such nice curls.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.710
You should see them when it rains.
Looks like a bomb went off.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.220
It's the same for me.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:27.770
But they're soft as a baby's curls
and such a lovely shade of red.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.730
You're making me blush.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.100
Where do you usually get your hair done?

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.650
My roommate cuts it for me.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.730
What kind of hair does your roommate have?

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.860
She's got silky black hair.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.070
You think she'd like a mohawk?

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.780
I have no idea...

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.130
Hey, Jada.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.880
Have you been doing this for a long time?

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.010
Let me think...

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:08.560
I opened shop three years ago.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.850
But even since before leaving home,
I've been playing with people's hair.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.770
I knew it. That totally explains it.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.570
The moment you started to work,
it felt like your whole attitude changed.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.410
Hm? Jada?

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.080
Hold on. I think I'm going to give you that mohawk after all!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.290
I'm sorry. Please don't.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:39.920
Hey, Ojou-san. I'm done.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.130
Here comes the mohawk!

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.430
How is it?

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.730
Wow! It looks great!

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.310
Right?

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:01.070
You really are a beautician, huh?

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.950
I won't deny it. I actually am a beautician.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.160
I'm gonna bring my roommate here with me next time!

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:10.200
I take sporadic days off,
so I can't promise I'll be open.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.700
Oh yeah. Jada?

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:13.960
What?

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.210
Do you mind if I come back over even if I don't need a haircut?

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.210
Hakumei, move back for a second.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.970
I'll tell you a secret about my house.
Keep it to yourself, okay?

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.100
A screw?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.560
That's why it doesn't topple over.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.980
Ah, I see.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:42.690
Come whenever you like.
I'll pull out all the stops for you!

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.570
Won't you roll away if you do?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.990
I'm home.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.910
Welcome back.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.000
Wow, you look nice and light!

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:08.970
Hey, Hakumei! How's it lookin' up there?

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:12.350
The reinforcement work all looks good.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:15.020
All right, then. I guess that's it for the day.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.230
Here. Wipe yourself off.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:23.730
The mortaring on the third windmill is looking pretty meager.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.740
We should fix it while it's still warm out.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.530
Well, we can forget it for now. One more day over.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.990
Good work.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.740
Hey, Iwashi!

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:34.410
Let's go grab a drink!

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:39.250
I'm good. I'm gonna go home and sleep.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.880
What?

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:44.710
That's your excuse every time.
We never end up going drinking!

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:49.880
Work makes me so tired that I'd probably fall asleep at the bar.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.140
Then how about on our day off?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.470
We'll miss the bus if we don't get a move on.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.480
Mikochi.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:05.900
Oh my, Hakumei. And your master, too.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:09.780
Sure has been a while.
On the way home from shopping?

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:13.910
Yes. I picked up some things while I was out negotiating with a new tea shop.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.580
Hmm...

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:19.960
Mikochi, let's go do something in town tomorrow.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.290
You're coming too, Iwashi!

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:22.120
Huh?!

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.580
That sounds nice.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.300
I know exactly where we should go for lunch, too.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.050
No, I don't think...

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.800
Oh, did you have someplace in mind yourself?

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.970
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.930
We'll meet at the grand staircase at noon, okay?

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.690
Thanks, Mikochi! You made it a cinch.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:55.240
Oh, there he is!

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.080
Sorry, I guess I slept in.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.960
Treat us to lunch and we'll call it even.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:07.800
I don't remember you ever buying <i>me</i> lunch after coming in late.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:12.220
I was just messing with you. Let's go! I'm starving!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.930
So, what're we gonna eat?

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.810
We'll head to the Toni neighborhood at Mustard Park.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.730
Hey, Iwashi...

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.860
Where do you usually do your shopping?

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.280
At the store in front of my home.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.990
What about for clothes?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:35.660
I already have my one outfit.
No need for anything more.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.120
Master.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:42.500
Let me take your measurements sometime, okay?

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.000
O-Okay...

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.000
Look, here we are!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:56.140
Sure is different. Lots of large customers about.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.260
I think the manager's a stout.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.760
Hup.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:03.020
These wide seats are a godsend.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.270
Three beers, and...

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:08.730
So where's this Mustard Park?

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:11.360
Oh, we're sitting in it right now.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.070
It's just the name of the place.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:17.450
They built over it, then?

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.780
Twenty years ago.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:22.040
You really don't come to the city much, do you?

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.040
Pickles.
You really don't come to the city much, do you?

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.000
Iwashi, do you want anything else?

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.130
Alcohol and grub.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.800
Ultra-Spicy Chili Potatoes.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.550
Thank you for waiting!

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.180
Okay, here goes...

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.260
To Iwashi's city debut!

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.810
And to getting those windmills serviced, too.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.430
Cheers!

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:51.150
Whoa, this is delicious.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.690
It's a real peculiar taste.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:56.320
They've mixed in some herbs with this beer, haven't they?

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:03.370
Hey, I wouldn't call this "Ultra Spicy"...

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.790
Another beer!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.330
Of course!

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.840
It's not what I'm used to,
but everything's damned good.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:19.590
I know! It's all part of the
"Iwashi probably wouldn't come here" tour!

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:21.390
First I'm hearing of that.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:25.430
Just go with the flow.
Have some mustard pickles.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:26.390
Will do.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.770
Try putting some in your burrito.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:30.810
Like this?

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.700
Can I get one more of these to go?

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.610
Glad you like them.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:43.990
Oh yeah, Hakumei...

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.660
We need to do that repointing on the windmills, right?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:51.330
You're seriously gonna talk shop while we're eating like this?

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:54.670
It just came to me.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.340
Well, then...

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.300
About the ratio of sand...

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.220
Yeah.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.350
Just one bit higher might help...

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.730
I'm stuffed!

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:10.390
Not exactly a light lunch, was it?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:15.150
There sure are a lot of clothing stores around here.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:18.280
This looks like a second-hand shop.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.410
Want to take a little peek inside?

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.160
Hey, come on in.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:31.830
We've got vintage clothes. Extra large pieces. And plenty of good brands, too.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:32.670
Huh...

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:40.930
Look at this kaftan! Crafted by Night Snail, the Needle Princess! Everything she does is a super-limited release!

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:45.550
So, a worthy buyer finally arrives to whisk this piece away.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:49.430
You're looking at the real thing there. Expensive, though.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:52.440
Hakumei! We're going to hunt down everything they've got!

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.110
Find clothes that have the snail design on it!

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.190
Understood!

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.110
Onii-san.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:11:59.990
Yeah?

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.610
There's something I'd really like you to buy.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.030
Straight to the point, huh?

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:10.450
Such an unexpected harvest!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.670
Great job.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:16.130
It totally suits you!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.460
It totally doesn't!

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.960
Which one is it?

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.260
That's a "Night Snail" piece as well.

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.380
Oh?

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.180
Whoa, this is expensive!

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:27.140
You're paying for quality, you know.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.770
Um, I really can't justify...

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:30.980
Now, hold on.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:37.480
It's as if that thing is clinging to your body!
The outfit's taken a liking to you.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:39.480
And you like it too, right?

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:46.030
Hakumei, Mikochi... we're gonna haggle.

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:46.950
Right!

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.240
Huh?!

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:50.620
Now, where were we?

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.290
Make it cheaper!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.080
We'll take all this—if you give us 20% off!

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:55.620
Throw in this scarf, would ya?

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.670
50,000! Will you take 50,000?!

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:01.510
No way! That's nearly half price!

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.380
You really think I can pay more than that for work clothes?

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.930
You're planning on working in that?!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.260
Master...

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:12.270
I'll make you some work clothes.
Please, anything but that.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.690
Uh, okay...

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:21.780
Damn! That guy knows how to drive a deal home.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.530
We found some great stuff!

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:28.700
Still, I don't think I'm gonna get used to wearing this type o' thing.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:32.540
Don't worry. It looks wonderful on you.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.200
Let's head to the next stop!

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:41.800
So that's the pine cricket fountain?

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.880
It's a pretty well-known tourist attraction.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.930
What are they up to over there?

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.300
Throwing coins.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:51.430
Ready, and...

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:52.720
Go!

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:56.980
They say that if you hit the antenna,
your business will flourish.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:00.610
That antenna on the other side is hardly nicked at all.

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:02.110
It's really tough to hit that one.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:05.240
It's a lot thinner than the one on this side, apparently.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:10.370
I saw a guy hit the one in the back with one throw before.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.740
It was amazing!

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:20.750
He was a master carpenter, and before he threw it,
he announced "one clean strike" in such a cool way!

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.000
Oh...

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:26.920
What are you gonna do? Can't back down now, Iwashi.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:28.760
Guess you're right.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.060
Great!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:42.480
I can throw as many as I want, yeah?

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.520
Sure!

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:47.190
Aw, that was close.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.570
Which one do you recommend?

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.030
The one with molasses sugar is popular.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:56.200
Think he'll hit it?

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.040
Who knows?

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:58.580
Maybe at this angle?

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:01.040
He'll probably keep going 'til he does.
Maybe at this angle?

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.590
He looks ready to throw away his life's savings.

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.050
Hakumei.

00:15:10.800 --> 00:15:12.850
Lend me some change.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:13.850
Sure thing.

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:25.730
Do you want to find something
that you think you'd like for dinner?

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:28.530
No need to fuss over me, you know.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:31.530
Finding shops is the real charm
of walking around the city.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:40.330
Ah! The Kamitori Bar!

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:43.540
They serve homemade food from every nation.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:49.670
Their lotus root dishes are all sublime!
But it might be a bit tight in there...

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:51.970
Well, we can just...

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:53.140
Iwashi.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:58.220
You were just looking at the mortaring, weren't you?

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:02.640
Sorry.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.560
That's nothing to be sorry about.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.320
Our best efforts have failed, huh?

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:08.980
Nothing else to do except...

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:17.330
Hakumei, the oden is freshly made!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.120
The croquettes are piping hot, too!

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.830
I'll take some of both!

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.330
You wanted the sweet miso shellfish soup and the garlic chive tsukudani, right?

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.840
That's right. Could I also get a bottle of Kuragakoi sake?

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.880
You're still not done?

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:32.340
Yeah. Hold this.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.640
This place sells the best chocolate!

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:36.720
What? Let's grab some, Hakumei!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.980
You really want to eat out here?

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:49.110
Come on, Iwashi! Let's waste the night away!

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:52.740
In the end, jabbering about work is how you want to spend your day off, huh?

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:59.830
Well, if you put it that way...

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:08.170
And get this! He'd made a mistake
and put <i>salt</i> in the mortar!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.500
No wonder it was salty!

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:16.130
But then I thought that them types of guys are the ones that come up with crazy inventions, right?

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.010
You said it!

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:24.640
Ah, the clouds are going round and round...

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:27.730
I hope we'll have enough alcohol.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:30.440
Should we try and put salt in ours too, Iwashi?

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:33.740
We gotta put somethin' even crazier in it!

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.400
All right! Let's do soup stock!

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:36.240
Soup stock...

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:48.290
Hey, Hakumei. You can go home now.

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:50.750
Great job today.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:51.750
You too.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:54.800
We might have to repoint this bridge, too.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.720
Speakin' of, Hakumei.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:58.800
Yeah?

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:04.060
On the way here today,
I found a bar that might be worth a look.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.070
You buying?

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:16.650
Hey... you know you were late again today, right?

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:28.540
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:36.340
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:40.340
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:44.310
the stars twinkle and shine

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:48.850
After we take in an easy breath,

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:53.230
the banquet will begin!

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:56.820
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:18:56.820 --> 00:19:00.570
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:04.490
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:09.330
It's itching to dance with us

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:13.290
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:17.260
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:22.550
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:26.100
At least, that's how we're feeling

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:41.530
Hm? A haircut?

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.370
I'm taking the day off today.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:45.200
What?!

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.240
Won't you reconsider?

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:50.370
Hakumei! Good to see you again.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:51.500
Heya.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.460
Are you even listening?!

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:58.550
Well the thing is... Here, try this.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:19:59.800
Liquor?

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:05.470
Sure is. It's homemade limoncello.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.270
I need your honest opinion.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:15.230
Hmm. It's sour... sickly sweet... bitter...

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:16.940
It's gross.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:21.110
Yep, it sure is. All that time spent making it, wasted...

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:24.240
My motivation has taken a nosedive.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.240
Let me have a sip.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:32.250
Aha! I know what went wrong here.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:39.710
When you added the lemon peel to the spirits,
did you add the white part as well?

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.130
Now that you mention it...

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:45.390
That's why it's so bitter.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:49.260
But my mother said that the white part
was good for the body.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:52.680
Well... That <i>is</i> true...

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:54.100
Hold it!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:57.520
What about my haircut?

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.570
It's motivation...

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:08.280
I have none.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:15.920
Do you still have ingredients?
I'll teach you how to make it.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.880
Would you really?

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:20.210
If we all help, it'll be done in no time.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:20.920
Ah, I'd be so grateful!

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:22.300
Um, for now, let's get the ingredients.
Ah, I'd be so grateful!

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:23.800
Cheer up.
Um, for now, let's get the ingredients.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.930
If this is what we're doing,
I'll help carry it out to perfection!
Um, for now, let's get the ingredients.

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:27.890
If this is what we're doing,
I'll help carry it out to perfection!

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:32.640
First of all, let's wash the skin in the river.

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.440
You may leave that to me!
You may leave that to me!

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:35.560
You may leave that to me!

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:36.520
Watch your step on the bank.
You may leave that to me!

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:39.400
Konju!
Watch your step on the bank.
You may leave that to me!

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:43.690
Then, peel the skin as thinly as possible.

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:47.530
Thinly, okay?

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:52.620
Soak the peeled skin in the spirits.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:22:00.880
Later, we'll drain it in a colander and add sugared water to taste. That's it!

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.670
How long do we wait?

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:09.260
It needs to soak for a week. After we add the ingredients, another week, I suppose?

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:13.850
So I have to wait two weeks for my haircut?

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:14.890
What?

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:21.610
She probably thought you'd cut her hair after we finished making it.

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:24.400
Is that what this is about?

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:28.200
Stop your crying, Ojou-san.

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:34.370
I'll give you something else as thanks for helping out.

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:39.920
Okay, all done!

00:22:40.960 --> 00:22:43.420
You can look in the mirror now!

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:53.470
How cute!

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:56.140
You really are a beautician, huh.

00:22:56.140 --> 00:23:01.100
No point in hiding it now. I really am a beautician.

00:23:02.020 --> 00:23:04.230
Sorry I only styled it.

00:23:04.230 --> 00:23:07.190
Ah, no, it's fine.

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:12.870
I had a bit to drink today, so I can't handle scissors.

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:15.660
Come back again when I've sobered up.

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:19.250
I'll be back before two weeks are up.

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:34.300
The dumplings that I ate this morning were hard,

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:35.930
so I'm taking the day off.
